  "interpretations": {
    "factual": "Three Rosanjin masthead digital copies have stronger static wide-narrow contrast and heavier normalized typical ink sections than Noto TC Song/Sans and AR PL Big5 Kaiti under matched text and both geometric alignments.",
    "hypothesis": "The weighting and differentiation of certain letterforming strokes might contribute to visual authorial intent, but the present global measurements cannot indicate WHICH meaningful stroke to emphasize, or WHY. The property may also be generic to other calligraphic styles.",
    "critical_negative": "Previous R2 attempted width transfer to new characters and produced no credible art-quality improvement. Therefore this new result does not license more angle-based, length-based or uniform thickening iterations.",
    "process_visibility": "Neither a digitized SVG nor regional width percentiles determine historical human pen motion, pressure, strokes or creative intent.",
    "remaining_unknown": "Whether per-stroke role or character-level asymmetry distinguishes this author from other excellent professional calligraphers, and whether any inferred design action is reusable."
  },
